  "overview": {
    "en": "Freeman Dyson was a British-American theoretical physicist and mathematician who unified the competing formulations of quantum electrodynamics by Schwinger, Tomonaga, and Feynman. He made wide-ranging contributions to physics, mathematics, and futuristic engineering concepts.",
    "es": "",
    "pt": "",
    "fr": "",
    "de": "",
    "zh": "",
